sub:assertion {
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/thompson1917-ch15-08> delphi:hasAssessment <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/thompson1917-ch15-08--grok> .
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/thompson1917-ch15-08--grok> a delphi:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Grok 4.7 on thompson1917-ch15-08: resolvable-now, resolvability 0.82" ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/dataset-resolvability-0.2.0> ;
    delphi:assessmentType "dataset-resolvability/0.2.0" ;
    delphi:hasScore "0.818"^^xsd:double ;
    delphi:hasVerdict "resolvable-now" ;
    delphi:hasConfidence "0.8"^^xsd:double ;
    dct:description "The claim denies that lateral versus terminal spines mark separate species and treats the spine as a mechanical variant produced in the uterus. Reference sequences of both named parasites are public and are tied to strains whose egg morphology is known, which is enough to test conspecificity without relying on the spine alone. Whether a funnel-shaped ootype moulds the spine is a narrower anatomical question and is not what the sequence data decide; the species claim itself is resolvable with existing genomic records." ;
    rdfs:comment "Proposed test with existing data: Link egg-spine position to sequence-based clusters of the adults that produced the eggs. One mechanically varying species is supported if lateral- and terminal-spined eggs are intermixed within one genomic lineage; two species are supported if spine position tracks deep, reciprocally monophyletic groups corresponding to S. haematobium and S. mansoni. The moulding hypothesis can be examined separately from the species question only with ootype anatomy." ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/agent/delphisci-resolvability-assessor-grok-4.7-high-fast> ;
    delphi:evidenceAgainst "Spine position was historically part of the species diagnosis, so early morphology-only assignments are partly circular.", "Ootype shape, the proposed mould, is anatomical description rather than a row in the sequence archives." ;
    delphi:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/thompson1917-ch15-08--grok--dataset-1>, <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/thompson1917-ch15-08--grok--dataset-2> .
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/thompson1917-ch15-08--grok--operationalizability> a delphi:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Operationalizability of thompson1917-ch15-08 by Grok 4.7: 0.86" ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/dataset-resolvability-0.2.0-operationalizability> ;
    delphi:assessmentType "dataset-resolvability/0.2.0/operationalizability" ;
    delphi:hasScore "0.86"^^xsd:double ;
